-- The hall (the book's map of Noke's Tower, the big round platform), redrawn in our pieces, twenty feet
-- up. As the map has it: the dining room with its kitchen corner to the north-west, the sitting room to the
-- south-west, and the library and lab filling the east half. The door from the garden's bridge is in the
-- south-east, the slope up to the bedroom in the south-west. The round wall is an octagon on our mat.

